course: dictionary
lesson: 4822
title: One word, two meanings: hunting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so you need context to know which one the writer means. «The common pheasant in British fields was brought from Asia long ago for hunting.» The words fields and pheasant are clues. Here hunting means chasing and killing wild animals.
explain: «Job hunting means searching adverts and sending applications, often dozens before getting anywhere.» Nobody is chasing animals here. Hunting means looking hard for something, in this case a job. Try your meaning in the sentence: "looking hard for a job" still makes sense, so you have found the right one.
explain: Hunting also describes how predators catch their prey. «It is just what your kitten does with a box or a ball of string, because play and searching are practice for hunting.» The kitten is not hunting for something lost. It is practising how to catch food.
fact: Hunting can mean chasing and killing wild animals for food, for sport, or to control their numbers.
fact: Hunting for something means looking hard for it, as in «house hunting» or «hunting for my shoe».
fact: Predators like lions, owls, sharks and spiders survive by hunting prey.
fact: «Whaling, the hunting of whales for oil and meat, nearly wiped out some species.»
fact: Many places have rules for hunting to protect animals, and hunting some animals, like tigers or rhinos, is banned.
exercise: «Job hunting means searching adverts and sending applications.» What does hunting mean here? | Playing with a ball of string | Chasing and killing wild animals | Catching prey for food | *Looking hard for something
exercise: Predators survive by doing what? | Eating only plants | Hiding from the wind | *Hunting prey | Sleeping all day in the sun
exercise: «Whaling, the hunting of whales for oil and meat, nearly wiped out some species.» What is the hunting in this sentence? | Counting whales in the sea | *Chasing and killing whales for oil and meat | Looking for a lost whale | Swimming alongside whales
test: «Treasure hunting» is a fun game of searching for hidden things. What does hunting mean in this phrase? | *Looking hard for something | Chasing wild animals | Killing animals for sport | Catching prey for food
test: Some animals hunt alone and some hunt in packs. What does hunting mean here? | Sitting still and waiting | Looking for a lost toy | Resting in the shade | *Chasing and catching prey for food
exam: «Hunting is how predators catch their prey.» Which sentence uses hunting in the same way? | We went to an egg hunt on Sunday | House hunting is tiring work | *Owls spend the night hunting mice | I spent an hour hunting for my keys
